    "markdown": "Course map for first assessment 2025. Organize learning across molecules, cells, organisms and ecosystems. This is a topic reference, not every assessed understanding; shared topics may include additional HL material.\n\n# A. Unity and diversity\n## Molecules and cells\nWater; nucleic acids; cellular structure.\n## Organisms and ecosystems\nOrganism diversity; evolution/speciation; biodiversity conservation.\n## Additional topics (HL)\nOrigins of cells; viruses; classification/cladistics.\n\n# B. Form and function\n## Molecules and cells\nCarbohydrates/lipids; proteins; membranes/transport; organelles/compartments; specialized cells.\n## Organisms and ecosystems\nGas exchange; transport; environmental adaptation; niches.\n## Movement (HL)\nMuscles and motility.\n\n# C. Interaction and interdependence\n## Molecules and cells\nEnzymes/metabolism; respiration; photosynthesis; neural signalling.\n## Organisms and ecosystems\nBody-system integration; immune defence; populations/communities; energy and matter flows.\n## Chemical signalling (HL)\n\n# D. Continuity and change\n## Molecules and cells\nDNA replication; protein production; mutation/gene editing; cell/nuclear division; water potential.\n## Organisms and ecosystems\nReproduction; inheritance; homeostasis; natural selection; sustainability/change; climate change.\n## Gene expression (HL)\n\n# Assessment\nPaper 1: 36%; paper 2: 44%; scientific investigation: 20%, maximum report length 3,000 words. Apply evidence, uncertainty and evaluation; avoid treating memorized definitions as sufficient preparation.\n## Examinations (SL)\nPaper 1: 90 minutes; paper 2: 90 minutes.\n## Examinations (HL)\nPaper 1: 120 minutes; paper 2: 150 minutes. HL also extends many shared topics; consult the guide for each statement's level.\n\n# Sources\n[IB course page](https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/curriculum/sciences/biology/)\n[IB subject brief, 2025](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/recognition/pdfs/dp_sciences_biology_subject-brief_jan_2022_e.pdf)"
