    "markdown": "First assessment 2024. Use this edition's briefs: some IB web-page prose still describes the previous course. Connect decisions to change, creativity, ethics and sustainability. Topic names below are a compact map, not all assessment requirements.\n\n# 1. Business foundations\nEntities, objectives, stakeholders, growth and multinational organizations.\n# 2. People at work\nHuman-resource management, structure, leadership, motivation and communication.\n## Organizational culture and employee relations (HL)\n# 3. Finance\nFunding, costs/revenue, accounts, profitability/liquidity, cash flow and investment appraisal.\n## Debt/equity ratios and budgets (HL)\n# 4. Marketing\nPlanning, research and the seven-P mix.\n## Sales forecasts and international marketing (HL)\n# 5. Operations\nMethods, location and break-even decisions.\n## Extended operations (HL)\nLean production/quality; production planning; contingency/crisis planning; R&D; management information systems.\n\n# Toolkit\nSelect tools that answer the decision in the case. Check the guide's level allocation; do not prescribe every available tool for every answer.\n\n# Assessment\nBoth levels complete a business research project, maximum 1,800 words, using a conceptual lens. Link evidence to the specific organization; avoid generic recommendations.\n## Papers and IA (SL)\nPaper 1: 90 minutes, 35%; paper 2: 90 minutes, 35%; IA: 30%.\n## Papers and IA (HL)\nPaper 1: 90 minutes, 25%; paper 2: 105 minutes, 30%; paper 3: 75 minutes, 25%; IA: 20%. Paper 3 addresses a social enterprise.\n\n# Sources\n[IB SL brief](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/programmes/dp/pdfs/business-management-sl-subject-brief-en.pdf)\n[IB HL brief](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/programmes/dp/pdfs/business-management-hl-subject-brief-en.pdf)"
