    "markdown": "For the Language A literature route, first assessment 2021. This is a compact reference; get the student's actual reading list before choosing texts or quotations.\n\n# Reading and interpretation\nStudy literary craft, readers' interpretations, historical/cultural contexts and relationships between texts. Trace how choices create effects; avoid replacing analysis with plot summary.\n# Assessment\nPaper 1 analyzes unseen literature; paper 2 compares two studied works. The oral connects two literary works through a global issue, including a work in translation.\n## Assessment (SL)\nPaper 1: 35%; paper 2: 35%; oral: 30%.\n## Assessment (HL)\nPaper 1: 35%; paper 2: 25%; oral: 20%; HL essay: 20%, 1,200–1,500 words on a studied work. HL has a larger reading programme.\n\n# Sources\n[IB literature brief](https://www.ibo.org/contentassets/5895a05412144fe890312bad52b17044/curriculum.brief-languagea.literature-eng.pdf)\n[IB literature course page](https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/curriculum/language-and-literature/language-a-literature/)"
