    "markdown": "First assessment 2026; both SL and HL exist. Earlier SL-only specifications are unsuitable. This map combines scientific and societal inquiry; individual guide statements still determine precise SL/HL boundaries.\n\n# 1. Foundations\nPerspectives, systems and sustainability are organizing concepts throughout the course.\n# 2. Ecology\n# 3. Biodiversity and conservation\n# 4. Water\n# 5. Land\n# 6. Atmosphere and climate\n# 7. Natural resources\n# 8. Population and urban systems\n\n# Additional lenses (HL)\nEnvironmental law; environmental/ecological economics; environmental ethics. Apply these lenses across topics and include the additional HL understandings, not just a separate revision block.\n\n# Assessment\nUse case studies and data to connect causes, consequences and management decisions. The investigation uses a report of at most 3,000 words. The practical programme includes a collaborative sciences project.\n## Papers and IA (SL)\nPaper 1: 60 minutes, 25%; paper 2: 120 minutes, 50%; investigation: 25%.\n## Papers and IA (HL)\nPaper 1: 120 minutes, 30%; paper 2: 150 minutes, 50%; investigation: 20%.\n\n# Sources\n[IB course page](https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/curriculum/sciences/environmental-systems-and-societies/)\n[IB subject brief, 2026](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/university-admission/pdfs/environmental-systems-and-societies-subject-brief-en.pdf)"
