    "markdown": "For assessment from 2027; no SL/HL. This is a research process reference, not a subject-specific guide. For examinations ending in 2026, obtain the earlier guide instead of applying the revised criteria.\n\n# Pathway and research question\nChoose subject-focused or interdisciplinary research using approved DP subjects. Establish scope, feasibility, disciplinary methods and a question that can be answered with available evidence.\n# Research and argument\nRecord source details, evaluate evidence and connect each analytical step to the question. Revise the scope when the evidence warrants it; distinguish findings from unsupported assumptions.\n# Structure\nTitle page, contents, introduction, analytical body, conclusion and references/bibliography. The essay limit is 4,000 words. Check the guide's detailed inclusion/exclusion rules before counting.\n# Reflection\nThree formal supervisor meetings, ending in a viva voce. Submit a final reflective statement of at most 500 words on the Reflection and progress form. Discuss decisions, learning and transfer rather than a task diary.\n# Assessment\nRevised criteria: framework; knowledge/understanding; analysis/argument; discussion/evaluation; reflection. Do not use the previous focus/method, critical-thinking, presentation and engagement rubric. Supervisor deadlines and subject-specific requirements take precedence over a generic checklist.\n\n# Sources\n[IB subject brief, 2027](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/university-admission/pdfs/ee_subjectbrief_en.pdf)\n[IB curriculum update](https://www.ibo.org/university-admission/latest-curriculum-updates/dp-extended-essay-updates/)"
