    "markdown": "Beginner French, SL only; assessment 2020–2028. This outline does not substitute for the language-specific syllabus.\n\n# Themes and topics\nIdentities: attributes, relationships, food/drink, physical well-being.\nExperiences: routine, leisure, holidays, festivals.\nHuman ingenuity: transport, entertainment, media, technology.\nSocial organization: neighbourhood, education, workplace, social issues.\nSharing the planet: climate, geography, environment, global issues.\n# Communication\nUse short, achievable listening, reading, writing and speaking tasks in French. Scaffold vocabulary and sentence construction, then gradually remove support.\n# Assessment\nWriting: 25%; listening: 25%; reading: 25%; individual oral: 25%. The oral uses a visual stimulus, discussion and a conversation across themes. There is no HL route.\n\n# Sources\n[IB ab initio brief](https://www.ibo.org/contentassets/5895a05412144fe890312bad52b17044/lang-ab-initio-2018-en.pdf)\n[IB ab initio course page](https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/curriculum/language-acquisition/language-ab-initio/)\n[IB subject availability](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/programmes/dp/pdfs/all-dp-subjects-list-en.pdf)"
