    "markdown": "For examinations through 2027. This is the most recent history edition within the first-assessment-2027 cutoff used by this catalogue. Confirm the school's chosen options before planning.\n\n# Prescribed subject\nChoose one: military leaders; conquest; move to global war; rights/protest; conflict/intervention.\n# World-history topics\nChoose two. Available areas include medieval societies/wars/rulers; early-modern transitions/states/wars; industrialization; independence; democratic states; authoritarian states; twentieth-century wars; Cold War. Confirm the school's topics and required examples from different regions.\n# Regional depth study (HL)\nOne regional option, with three sections: Africa/Middle East, Americas, Asia/Oceania or Europe.\n# Historical investigation\nIA maximum 2,200 words: source identification/evaluation, investigation and reflection. This is the older investigation structure.\n\n# Assessment\nPractise source analysis separately from comparative essays. Build arguments around evidence and evaluate interpretations; a chronological narrative alone is insufficient.\n## Papers and IA (SL)\nPaper 1: 60 minutes, 30%; paper 2: 90 minutes, 45%; IA: 25%.\n## Papers and IA (HL)\nPaper 1: 60 minutes, 20%; paper 2: 90 minutes, 25%; paper 3: 150 minutes, 35%; IA: 20%.\n\n# Sources\n[IB History SL brief](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/programmes/dp/pdfs/history-sl-2020-eng.pdf)\n[IB History HL brief](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/programmes/dp/pdfs/history-hl-2020-eng.pdf)"
