    "markdown": "First assessment 2021; current assessment through 2028. AA emphasizes reasoning and analytical fluency with and without technology. This is a compact map; use the guide's SL/AHL statement numbers for exact boundaries.\n\n# 1. Number and algebra\nScientific notation, sequences/series, financial applications, logarithms/exponentials, binomial expansion and proof.\n## Further algebra (HL)\nInduction and contradiction; complex numbers; further counting, series and algebra.\n# 2. Functions\nDomains/ranges, inverses/composition, transformations, quadratics, rational/exponential/logarithmic models and solving equations.\n## Further functions (HL)\nPolynomial structure, further rational functions, modulus and inequalities.\n# 3. Geometry and trigonometry\nMeasurement, radians, circular functions, identities and trigonometric equations.\n## Vectors and further trigonometry (HL)\nVector geometry, lines/planes and additional identities.\n# 4. Statistics and probability\nData, correlation/regression, probability, discrete random variables, binomial and normal models.\n## Further probability (HL)\nConditional probability/Bayes and continuous random variables.\n# 5. Calculus\nDifferentiation/integration, graph behaviour, optimization, area and motion.\n## Further calculus (HL)\nAdvanced methods, differential equations and Maclaurin expansions.\n\n# Assessment\nExploration: 20%; criteria assess presentation, communication, engagement, reflection and mathematics.\n## Examinations (SL)\nPaper 1: 90 minutes, 40%, no calculator; paper 2: 90 minutes, 40%, technology required.\n## Examinations (HL)\nPaper 1: 120 minutes, 30%, no calculator; paper 2: 120 minutes, 30%, technology required; paper 3: 60 minutes, 20%, technology required.\n\n# Sources\n[IB AA guide, 2021](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/university-admission/pdfs/subject-guides/mathematics-analysis-approaches-guide.pdf)\n[IB AA brief, 2021](https://www.ibo.org/contentassets/5895a05412144fe890312bad52b17044/subject-brief-dp-math-analysis-and-approaches-en.pdf)\n[IB edition dates](https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/curriculum/mathematics/)"
