    "markdown": "For assessment in 2021–2028. AI emphasizes modelling, statistics and technology-supported interpretation. It is distinct from AA and from discontinued Mathematical Studies. This map does not enumerate every SL/AHL statement.\n\n# 1. Number and algebra\nApproximation, sequences/series, financial applications, logarithms and numerical techniques.\n## Further algebra (HL)\nComplex numbers and matrices, including applications.\n# 2. Functions\nRepresentations, modelling, fitting, solving and interpreting functions in context.\n## Further models (HL)\nMore advanced function models and transformations.\n# 3. Geometry and trigonometry\nMeasurement, trigonometry, bearings, coordinates and Voronoi diagrams.\n## Vectors and graphs (HL)\nVector methods, graph theory and network applications.\n# 4. Statistics and probability\nSampling, descriptive statistics, correlation/regression, distributions and hypothesis tests.\n## Further statistics (HL)\nAdditional distributions, inference and tests. Confirm assumptions and the guide's test requirements before choosing a method.\n# 5. Calculus\nRates, optimization, integration and numerical approximations.\n## Further calculus (HL)\nDifferential-equation models, Euler approximations and further integration.\n\n# Assessment\nExploration: 20%, with presentation/communication/engagement/reflection/mathematics criteria. Make assumptions and model limitations explicit.\n## Examinations (SL)\nPaper 1: 90 minutes, 40%; paper 2: 90 minutes, 40%. Technology required in both.\n## Examinations (HL)\nPapers 1 and 2: 120 minutes each, 30% each; paper 3: 60 minutes, 20%. Technology required throughout.\n\n# Sources\n[IB AI guide, 2021](https://ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/university-admission/pdfs/dp-mathematics-applications-and-interpretation-guide-en.pdf)\n[IB AI brief, 2021](https://www.ibo.org/contentassets/5895a05412144fe890312bad52b17044/subject-brief-dp-math-applications-and-interpretations-en.pdf)\n[IB edition dates](https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/curriculum/mathematics/)"
