    "markdown": "First assessed in 2025. A concise course map, not the complete guide. Shared topics can contain additional HL depth; a shared heading does not make every treatment SL. Use the class guide for fine-grained boundaries.\n\n# A. Motion and spacetime\n## A.1 Kinematics\nMotion graphs and mathematical models.\n## A.2 Forces and momentum\nForce diagrams, interactions and conservation.\n## A.3 Energy, work and power\nTrack transfers and check units.\n## A.4 Rotation (HL)\nRigid-body mechanics.\n## A.5 Relativity (HL)\nGalilean and special relativity.\n\n# B. Matter and thermal physics\n## B.1 Thermal transfers\n## B.2 Greenhouse effect\n## B.3 Gas models\n## B.4 Thermodynamics (HL)\n## B.5 Electrical circuits\n\n# C. Waves\n## C.1 Oscillations\n## C.2 Wave models\n## C.3 Wave effects\n## C.4 Standing waves and resonance\n## C.5 Doppler shifts\n\n# D. Fields\n## D.1 Gravity\n## D.2 Electric and magnetic fields\n## D.3 Charged-particle motion\n## D.4 Electromagnetic induction (HL)\n\n# E. Atomic, nuclear and quantum physics\n## E.1 Atomic structure\n## E.2 Quantum physics (HL)\n## E.3 Radioactivity\n## E.4 Nuclear fission\n## E.5 Fusion and stellar physics\n\n# Assessment\nPaper 1: 36%; paper 2: 44%; investigation: 20%, report at most 3,000 words. No separate options paper. Integrate uncertainty, experimental design and evaluation into practice.\n## Examinations (SL)\nPaper 1: 90 minutes; paper 2: 90 minutes.\n## Examinations (HL)\nPaper 1: 120 minutes; paper 2: 150 minutes. Shared C.1/C.3/C.5, D.1/D.2 and E.1/E.3 also have HL extensions.\n\n# Sources\n[IB course page](https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/curriculum/sciences/physics/)\n[IB subject brief, 2025](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/recognition/pdfs/dp_sciences_physics_subject-brief_jan_2022_e.pdf)"
