    "markdown": "For examinations from 2027. This replaces the earlier options-based course and experimental-replication IA. Integrate concepts, content and contexts rather than learning isolated study summaries.\n\n# Concepts\nBias, causality, change, measurement, perspective and responsibility.\n# Content\nBiological, cognitive and sociocultural explanations of behaviour, with research methodology.\n# Contexts\nHealth/well-being; human development; human relationships; learning/cognition. All four are studied, with class practicals integrated across them.\n# Class practicals\nAt least four. Practise design decisions, ethics, interpreting findings and evaluating claims. Retrieve the class's actual practicals rather than inventing what the student did.\n# Extensions (HL)\nCulture, motivation and technology as influences on behaviour; analysis and interpretation of research data.\n\n# Assessment\nIA: a research proposal for a specified population; not conducting the previous course's replication. Use evidence to justify method and ethical choices.\n## Papers and IA (SL)\nPaper 1: 90 minutes, 35%; paper 2: 90 minutes, 35%; IA: 30%.\n## Papers and IA (HL)\nPaper 1: 90 minutes, 25%; paper 2: 90 minutes, 25%; paper 3: 105 minutes, 30%; IA: 20%.\n\n# Sources\n[IB Psychology guide, 2027](https://ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/university-admission/pdfs/subject-guides/psychology-first-assessment-2027-guide-sbs.pdf)\n[IB subject brief, 2027](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/programmes/dp/pdfs/dp_psychology_subjectbrief_en.pdf)"
