    "markdown": "For the Language A language-and-literature route, first assessment 2021. Distinct from literature-only and Language B. Retrieve the school's works and non-literary bodies of work before giving text-specific advice.\n\n# Texts and meaning\nAnalyze literary and non-literary communication through form, audience, purpose and context. Explore interpretation, time/place and connections between texts. Support each claim with precise textual evidence.\n# Assessment\nPaper 1 uses unseen non-literary material; paper 2 compares two studied literary works. The oral links literature and a non-literary body of work through a global issue.\n## Assessment (SL)\nPaper 1: 35%; paper 2: 35%; oral: 30%.\n## Assessment (HL)\nPaper 1: 35%; paper 2: 25%; oral: 20%; HL essay: 20%, 1,200–1,500 words on a studied work/body of work. HL includes a larger reading programme.\n\n# Sources\n[IB language-and-literature brief](https://www.ibo.org/contentassets/5895a05412144fe890312bad52b17044/curriculum.brief-languagea.language.and.literature-eng.pdf)\n[IB course page](https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/curriculum/language-and-literature/language-a-language-and-literature/)"
