    "markdown": "Language acquisition for learners with prior experience; assessment 2020–2028. This is a course map, not a language-specific grammar specification.\n\n# Themes\nIdentities; experiences; human ingenuity; social organization; sharing the planet. Topics within these themes are suggestions, not a prescribed checklist.\n# Communication\nPractise listening, reading, writing and conversation in Spanish. Match register and text type to the situation; explain corrections and let the student retry.\n# Assessment\nWriting: 25%; listening: 25%; reading: 25%; individual oral: 25%.\n## Oral and writing (SL)\nThe oral starts from a visual stimulus; writing tasks target SL proficiency.\n## Literature and oral (HL)\nStudy two works originally written in Spanish. The oral begins with a literary extract; expect greater linguistic complexity.\n\n# Sources\n[IB Language B brief](https://www.ibo.org/contentassets/5895a05412144fe890312bad52b17044/lang-b-2018-en.pdf)\n[IB Language B course page](https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/curriculum/language-acquisition/language-b/)\n[IB Language B guide](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/university-admission/pdfs/subject-guides/language-b-guide.pdf)"
