    "markdown": "Literature and performance in Spanish; SL only, first assessment 2024. This is an interdisciplinary literature/theatre course. Confirm the school's authorized language offering and chosen works.\n\n# Interpretation and performance\nConnect close reading with staging decisions. Explore audiences, cultural contexts and relationships between written and performed texts. Keep rehearsal notes tied to evidence from the work.\n# Assessment\nComparative essay examination: 30%; written assignment: 30%; transformative performance and individual oral: 40%. The assignment analyzes the student's performance choices in a dramatic extract. The transformative task stages non-dramatic literature.\n# Study guidance\nDescribe what an audience sees and hears, explain its textual basis and evaluate alternatives. Retrieve the student's own performance evidence before making specific claims about it.\n\n# Sources\n[IB current performance brief](https://www.ibo.org/globalassets/new-structure/programmes/dp/pdfs/lit-performance-subject-brief-en.pdf)\n[IB course page](https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/curriculum/language-and-literature/literature-and-performance/)"
